<article class="env-proposition" id="057F45">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/057F45">Proposition <span data-tag="057F45">8.2.8.7</span>.</a> Let $\mathbf{A}$ be a combinatorial model category, and let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calC '$ be a functor between small categories. Then: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The pair $( f_{!}, f^{\ast } )$ determines a Quillen adjunction between the <em>projective</em> model structures on $\Fun (\calC , \mathbf{A})$ and $\Fun (\calC ', \mathbf{A})$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
The pair $( f^{\ast }, f_{\ast } )$ determines a Quillen adjunction between the <em>injective</em> model structures on $\Fun (\calC , \mathbf{A})$ and $\Fun (\calC ', \mathbf{A})$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from the simple observation that $f^{\ast }$ preserves weak equivalences, projective fibrations, and weak cofibrations. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>